ty?* | `<concept>`, `<title>`, `<shortdesc>`, `<conbody>`, `<p>`, `<ul>`, `<section>` |\n| [02](/dita-tutorial/part-1-topics/stage-02-first-map) | `tutorial/02-first-map` | A one-topic guide map | `<map>`, `<topicref>`, relative paths, project root |\n| [03](/dita-tutorial/part-1-topics/stage-03-first-build) | `tutorial/03-first-build` | The first HTML guide | **Manage Deliverables**, DITA-OT, output inspection |\n| [04](/dita-tutorial/part-1-topics/stage-04-task-and-reference) | `tutorial/04-task-and-reference` | *Recording your first track*, *Supported audio formats* | `<task>`, `<steps>`, `<cmd>`, `<reference>`, CALS `<table>`; the three information types |\n| [05](/dita-tutorial/part-1-topics/stage-05-inline-and-block) | `tutorial/05-inline-and-block` | *What is digital audio?*, *Trimming audio* | `<uicontrol>`, `<menucascade>`, `<term>`, `<filepath>`, `<note>`, `<dl>`, `<ol>`, `<sl>`, `<fn>`, `<simpletable>`, `<codeblock>` |\n| [06](/dita-tutorial/part-1-topics/stage-06-rich-tasks) | `tutorial/06-rich-tasks` | *Installing Audacity*, *Exporting audio*, *Removing background noise*, *Preparing to record* | `<prereq>`, `<postreq>`, `<substeps>`, `<choices>`, `<choicetable>`, `<stepxmp>`, `<stepresult>`, `<steps-unordered>`, `<example>` |\n| [07](/dita-tutorial/part-1-topics/stage-07-links) | `tutorial/07-links` | Topics that point at each other | `<xref>`, `<related-links>`, `<link>`, `<linklist>`, `<linkpool>`, `<linktext>`, `<desc>` |\n| [08](/dita-tutorial/part-1-topics/stage-08-figures) | `tutorial/08-figures` | Illustrations, an inline SVG, an image map and an equation | `<fig>`, `<image>`, `<alt>`, `<imagemap>`, `<svg-container>`, `<equation-block>`, `<mathml>` |\n| [09](/dita-tutorial/part-2-maps/stage-09-map-structure) | `tutorial/09-map-structure` | Hierarchy, sequences and generated links | nested `<topicref>`, `@collection-type`, `@linking`, `@locktitle`, `<navtitle>`, `<topicgroup>`, `<reltable>` |\n| [10](/dita-tutorial/part-2-maps/stage-10-keys) | `tutorial/10-keys` | Product variables and indirect links | `<keydef>`, `<keyword keyref>`, `@keyref`, `@keys`, `<mapref>`, `<linktext>` |\n| [11](/dita-tutorial/part-2-maps/stage-11-reuse) | `tutorial/11-reuse` | Shared steps and notes | `@conref`, `@conrefend`, `@conkeyref`, conref push with `@conaction`, `@processing-role=\"resource-only\"` |\n| [12](/dita-tutorial/part-2-maps/stage-12-glossary) | `tutorial/12-glossary` | Glossary entries and abbreviations | `<glossentry>`, `<glossterm>`, `<glossdef>`, `<glossAlt>`, `<abbreviated-form>`, `<term keyref>`, `<glossgroup>` |\n| [13](/dita-tutorial/part-2-maps/stage-13-metadata-and-index) | `tutorial/13-metadata-and-index` | Prolog metadata and a real index | `<prolog>`, `<metadata>`, `<author>`, `<critdates>`, `<audience>`, `<indexterm>`, `<index-see>`; the metadata policy |\n| [14](/dita-tutorial/part-3-conditions/stage-14-conditional-text) | `tutorial/14-conditional-text` | Beginner and podcaster guides, per platform, and a review build | `@platform`, `@audience`, `@rev`, `<ph>` alternatives; DITAVAL `<prop action>`, `<revprop>`, `<startflag>`, `<style-conflict>`; one DITAVAL per deliverable |\n| [15](/dita-tutorial/part-3-conditions/stage-15-subject-scheme) | `tutorial/15-subject-scheme` | A controlled vocabulary for the conditions | `<subjectScheme>`, `<subjectdef>`, `<enumerationdef>`, `<attributedef>`, `<hasNarrower>`, `<mapref type=\"subjectScheme\">`; `validate-conditions` |\n| [16](/dita-tutorial/part-3-conditions/stage-16-branch-filtering) | `tutorial/16-branch-filtering` | Three install variants from one topic | `<ditavalref>`, `<ditavalmeta>`, `<dvrResourcePrefix>`, `<dvrResourceSuffix>`, `<dvrKeyscopePrefix>` |\n| [17](/dita-tutorial/part-3-conditions/stage-17-key-scopes) | `tutorial/17-key-scopes` | One collection of three guides | `@keyscope`, scoped keys, `<mapref scope=\"peer\">` |\n| [18](/dita-tutorial/part-3-conditions/stage-18-chunking-and-output) | `tutorial/18-chunking-and-output` | Control over pages and file names | `@chunk`, `@copy-to`, nested topics, `@print`, `@toc`, `@search`, `@outputclass`, `<topicset>`, `<topicsetref>` |\n| [19](/dita-tutorial/part-4-books/stage-19-bookmap) | `tutorial/19-bookmap` | The PDF book | `<bookmap>`, `<booktitle>`, `<bookmeta>`, `<frontmatter>`, `<booklists>`, `<part>`, `<chapter>`, `<appendix>`, `<backmatter>`; the `pdf` transtype |\n| [20](/dita-tutorial/part-4-books/stage-20-troubleshooting) | `tutorial/20-troubleshooting` | *The recording is silent* | `<troubleshooting>`, `<condition>`, `<troubleSolution>`, `<cause>`, `<remedy>`, `<steps-informal>`, `<note type=\"trouble\">` |\n| [21](/dita-tutorial/part-4-books/stage-21-hazards-and-safety) | `tutorial/21-hazards-and-safety` | Hearing-safety statements | `<hazardstatement>`, `<messagepanel>`, `<typeofhazard>`, `<consequence>`, `<howtoavoid>`, `<hazardsymbol>`; a conref'd hazard |\n| [22](/dita-tutorial/part-4-books/stage-22-software-domains) | `tutorial/22-software-domains` | Scripting Audacity from the command line | `<coderef>`, `<screen>`, `<userinput>`, `<systemoutput>`, `<cmdname>`, `<parmname>`, `<option>`, `<parml>`, `<msgblock>`, `<syntaxdiagram>`, `<properties>` |\n| [23](/dita-tutorial/part-4-books/stage-23-learning) | `tutorial/23-learning` | A \"check your understanding\" page | `<learningAssessment>`, `<lcObjectives>`, `<lcDuration>`, `<lcInteraction>`, `<lcTrueFalse2>`, `<lcSingleSelect2>`, `<lcMultipleSelect2>`, `<lcSequencing2>`; the check and the L&T DTDs |\n| [24](/dita-tutorial/part-5-governance/stage-24-drafts-and-localization) | `tutorial/24-drafts-and-localization` | Ready for review and translation | `@xml:lang`, `@translate`, `@dir`, `<sort-as>`, `<draft-comment>`, `<required-cleanup>`, `@status`, `<revised>`, `<change-historylist>` |\n| [25](/dita-tutorial/part-5-governance/stage-25-house-rules) | `tutorial/25-house-rules` | Rules as code | Schematron `house-style.sch`, **House Rules (Schematron)**, `AGENTS.md`, the house-style skill; house rules in the check |\n| [26](/dita-tutorial/part-5-governance/stage-26-final) | `tutorial/26-final` | The complete guide, tagged `tutorial/final` | Nothing new: every deliverable builds, the project is clean |\n\n## How to use it {#how-to-use-it}\n\n:::steps\n1. **Read [**How the tutorial works**](/dita-tutorial/start-here/how-the-tutorial-works)** One project, built stage by stage, with a checkpoint at each stage.\n2. [**Set up your tools**](/dita-tutorial/start-here/set-up) The DogsBay XML editor, which includes DITA-OT 4.3.5, and the empty `my-audacity-guide` folder.\n3. **Follow your chosen learning path** Each page lists prerequisites, provides source examples, and ends with checks. Write the files in `my-audacity-guide`. Use the checkpoint instructions when skipping optional modules; each lesson assumes the preceding stage's files.\n4. **Compare when you are stuck** Every page links to the GitHub compare view for its stage, which shows exactly what changed.\n:::\n\n**Time:** 10 to 40 minutes per stage, plus practice exercises. **You need:** the DogsBay XML editor. Git is optional.\n\nFollow the core course for topic authoring, maps, reuse, variants, and validation. Choose optional modules when you need their publishing features. Use the checkpoints in the learning path when skipping stages. Allow additional time for setup, troubleshooting, and the capstone.\n\n## Where to go next {#where-to-go-next}\n\n:::cards\n- **[Choose a learning path](/dita-tutorial/start-here/learning-path){icon=\"book-open\"}**\n  The core course, optional modules, and starting checkpoints.\n\n- **[How the tutorial works](/dita-tutorial/start-here/how-the-tutorial-works){icon=\"git-branch\"}**\n  One project, stage by stage, and the checkpoint branches.\n\n- **[Set up your tools](/dita-tutorial/start-here/set-up){icon=\"wrench\"}**\n  Install the DogsBay XML editor and its command line.\n\n- **[Stage 00: Create your project folder](/dita-tutorial/part-1-topics/stage-00-setup){icon=\"play\